{
  "intent": "general_information",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "text": "Why should observations of autistic preschoolers in inclusive classrooms record how teachers and peers respond, not just the child's behavior?",
      "required": true
    }
  ],
  "items": [
    {
      "item_id": "i1",
      "excerpt_id": "x-25115da8f57de6abfa66",
      "quote": "Since social interaction is a result of an exchange between at least two people, the behaviors of both interlocutors should ideally be analyzed. However, coding grids are often child-centered. Even though coding children's responses to adults presupposes an initiative on their part, information lacks precise modalities of solicitations and contributions to the sequence unfolding, the adjustments of children over time, and, therefore, the conditions that may favor their social engagement.",
      "relation": "direct",
      "stance": "supports",
      "claim_ids": [
        "c1"
      ],
      "scope_quotes": [
        {
          "field": "population",
          "excerpt_id": "x-25115da8f57de6abfa66",
          "quote": "autistic children in school settings"
        },
        {
          "field": "conditions",
          "excerpt_id": "x-25115da8f57de6abfa66",
          "quote": "inclusive preschool settings"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "item_id": "i2",
      "excerpt_id": "x-889afd2336d4642e6c19",
      "quote": "The coding grids mainly focus on autistic children while partners' behaviors (adults, peers) are often coded in less detail, thus providing little information on their dynamic role in the interactions.",
      "relation": "direct",
      "stance": "supports",
      "claim_ids": [
        "c1"
      ],
      "scope_quotes": [
        {
          "field": "population",
          "excerpt_id": "x-889afd2336d4642e6c19",
          "quote": "autistic preschool children in inclusive preschool settings"
        },
        {
          "field": "conditions",
          "excerpt_id": "x-889afd2336d4642e6c19",
          "quote": "inclusive preschool settings"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "item_id": "i3",
      "excerpt_id": "x-c3be127a874dec64cd87",
      "quote": "Our review highlights the importance of offering occasions for initiatives to autistic children and training of neurotypical peers to better interact with autistic children and promote verbal communication.",
